            <p>Obturator Foramen. This image highlights&#x000a0;the obturator foramen (red arrow), a large opening created by the ischium and pubis bones of the pelvis.&#x000a0;This aperture&#x000a0;serves as a passage for nerves and vessels to the lower limb. Contributed by Sunil Munakomi, MD</p>
          </caption>
